<title>USA: Illinois unemployment rates drops to 5.2 percent.</title>
<headline>Illinois unemployment rates drops to 5.2 percent.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Illinois' unemployment rate fell to 5.2 percent in September from 5.4 percent in August, the state's department of employment security reported Wednesday.</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted jobless figures for the state showed 320,251 unemployed workers in September, compared to 330,896 in August. In September 1995, Illinois' unemployment rate was 5.2 percent with 315,419 people without jobs.</p>
<p>--Karen Pierog, 312-408-8647</p>
